  "termsOfServiceSection01Title": "1. Acceptance",
  "termsOfServiceSection01Body": "Welcome to {appTitle} (“the Service”). Please read these Terms of Service (“the Terms”) before use.\nBy tapping agree, security verification up, security verification in, or using the Service, you agree to be bound by the Terms. If you disagree, stop using the Service.\nWe may update the Terms from time to time. Continued use after notice or updates means you accept the revised Terms.",
  "termsOfServiceSection02Title": "2. Description of the Service",
  "termsOfServiceSection02Body": "The Service combines local storage with blockchain-related features: you can create, edit, and manage notes on your device and optionally perform on-chain actions (such as transactions, hashes, or metadata—see in-app flows and prompts).\nCurrent characteristics may evolve with releases:\n• Local storage: note data is mainly stored on your device (e.g. local database); uninstalling the app may erase local data—back up on your own.\n• On-chain features: you may voluntarily submit on-chain operations for proof, sync, or display; on-chain records are often public and hard to delete.\n• Multi-chain: multiple EVM-compatible networks as listed in the app.\n• Note account: keys are generated or imported by you on the device; you are responsible for safeguarding keys and recovery phrases.\nThe Service provides technical tools only and does not warrant the legality, accuracy, completeness, or fitness for a particular purpose of your content.",
  "termsOfServiceSection03Title": "3. Note account and security",
  "termsOfServiceSection03Body": "3.1 Note account and credentials: after creating or importing an note account, the app manages addresses and key material on the device. Recovery phrases and security keys are among the only practical ways to recover notes—back them up offline and keep them secret.\n3.2 Your responsibility: actions performed while the app or note account is unlocked on your device are treated as yours or authorized by you. Losses from leaked phrases/keys, lost devices, malware, phishing, or failure to follow prompts are yours to bear.\n3.3 Security tips:\n• Never share your recovery phrase or security key with anyone\n• Use a strong app password and device lock / biometrics where available\n• Back up your phrase in a trusted environment and verify the backup\n• Beware of fake apps and phishing links\n3.4 We and our staff will never ask for your full recovery phrase or security key. Reject such requests and report them through official channels.",
  "@termsOfServiceSection04Body": {
    "placeholders": {
      "appTitle": {
        "type": "String"
      }
    }
  },
  "termsOfServiceSection04Title": "4. Blockchain transactions and fees",
  "termsOfServiceSection04Body": "4.1 Gas and network fees: on-chain transactions require fees paid to the network (e.g. gas). Fees are collected by the network, not by {appTitle} as a software provider on your behalf; amounts depend on the network and congestion.\n4.2 Confirmation time: transactions need network confirmation; timing depends on network conditions and your fee settings—we do not guarantee a specific duration.\n4.3 Failures and charges: insufficient balance, RPC errors, user cancellation, or contract reverts may cause failure; network fees already spent may be non-refundable per network rules.\n4.4 Irreversibility: once sufficiently confirmed, on-chain transactions usually cannot be undone. Double-check network, amounts, and contract calls before security verification and broadcasting.\n4.5 You are responsible for all on-chain actions you initiate. To the extent permitted by law, we are not liable for losses from blockchain protocols, nodes, smart contracts, or your own mistakes.",
  "termsOfServiceSection05Title": "5. Acceptable use",
  "termsOfServiceSection05Body": "You must not:\n• Create, upload, or distribute illegal, infringing, defamatory, obscene, violent, hateful, or otherwise unlawful content\n• Use the Service for fraud, money laundering, illegal fundraising, IP infringement, or other conduct prohibited by regulators\n• Access, probe, disrupt, or damage the Service or related infrastructure without authorization\n• Scrape, abuse APIs, or harm other users’ normal use (unless we agree in writing)\n• Send bulk harassment or unsolicited commercial messages\nIf you breach the above, we may warn you, restrict features, suspend, or terminate access, and cooperate with lawful or regulatory requests where required.",
  "termsOfServiceSection06Title": "6. Intellectual property",
  "termsOfServiceSection06Body": "6.1 The Service itself: client software, UI, branding, and documentation are protected by us or right holders. Without permission, you may not copy, reverse engineer, crack, or commercially redistribute the core software (except as allowed by law).\n6.2 Your content: you retain rights in notes and content you create; the Terms do not transfer those rights to us.\n6.3 License to us: solely to operate and improve the Service (sync, display, backup, on-chain submission, etc.), you grant us a non-exclusive, royalty-free license, revocable as permitted by the Terms.\n6.4 Do not use our trademarks, app name, or logos in a confusing way without written consent.",
  "termsOfServiceSection07Title": "7. Disclaimers",
  "termsOfServiceSection07Body": "7.1 “As is”: to the fullest extent permitted by law, the Service is provided “as is” and “as available.” We disclaim warranties of uninterrupted operation, error-free use, suitability for your needs, or compatibility with all devices or software.\n7.2 Data and security: we use reasonable measures but cannot guarantee there will never be data loss, leaks, or outages due to force majeure, lost devices, malware, attacks, or external systems (blockchain / IPFS, etc.).\n7.3 Third parties: the Service may rely on nodes, gateways, decentralized storage, push messaging, etc.; we do not warrant third parties’ availability, accuracy, or compliance—assess risks yourself.\n7.4 On-chain notes and protocol risks: on-chain notes and related protocols involve network issues, contract bugs, forks, and other risks—you assume them.\n7.5 Liability cap: except where law forbids, we are not liable for indirect, incidental, special, or consequential damages; our total liability is capped at fees you actually paid us for the disputed Service (zero if none).",
  "termsOfServiceSection08Title": "8. Changes, suspension, and termination",
  "termsOfServiceSection08Body": "8.1 We may change, suspend, or discontinue features for business, compliance, or technical reasons; we will notify you in-app when practicable.\n8.2 You may stop using the Service and uninstall at any time; export or back up important data beforehand.\n8.3 We may suspend or terminate access if you materially breach the Terms.\n8.4 After termination, unless the law requires otherwise, we have no obligation to retain or return data already on-chain, on third-party networks, or locally under your control.",
  "termsOfServiceSection09Title": "9. Governing law and disputes",
  "termsOfServiceSection09Body": "9.1 These Terms are governed by the laws of mainland China (for these Terms only, excluding conflict-of-law rules that would select foreign law, unless mandatory law says otherwise).\n9.2 Disputes should first be resolved through good-faith negotiation.\n9.3 If negotiation fails, either party may bring a suit in a court with jurisdiction (e.g. where our principal office is located), subject to mandatory jurisdictional rules.",
